@startuml StateMachine_BookingRequest_Lifecycle

title State Machine Diagram - BookingRequest Lifecycle\n(Temporary Lock Management)

[*] --> active : Request Booking\nBookingService.requestBooking()

state "active" as active #LightBlue {
    active : Temporary vehicle lock created
    active : 15-minute expiration timer running
    active : User can proceed to confirm
    active : Prevents other users from booking
}

state "confirmed" as confirmed #LightGreen {
    confirmed : User confirmed and created actual booking
    confirmed : Lock converted to real booking
    confirmed : BookingRequest archived
}

state "expired" as expired #LightGray {
    expired : 15-minute window elapsed
    expired : No confirmation from user
    expired : Lock released automatically
    expired : Vehicle becomes available again
}

state "canceled" as canceled #LightPink {
    canceled : Conflict detected during confirmation
    canceled : Or user abandoned the request
    canceled : Lock released manually
}

active --> confirmed : User Confirms\nBookingService.confirmBooking()\n[within 15 minutes]
note on link
    **Trigger:** User action
    **Precondition:** Token not expired
    **Action:** 
    1. Verify token valid
    2. Re-check conflicts
    3. Create actual Booking
    4. Update status = "confirmed"
end note

active --> expired : Time Elapsed\n[expiresAt < now]
note on link
    **Trigger:** Time-based
    **Condition:** 15 minutes passed
    
    **Action:**
    1. System checks expiration
    2. Update status = "expired"
    
    **TTL Index:** MongoDB auto-deletes
    after expiration
end note

active --> expired : TTL Index\n[MongoDB auto-cleanup]
note on link
    **Automatic Cleanup:**
    MongoDB TTL index removes
    document after expiresAt
    
    No manual intervention needed
end note

active --> canceled : Conflict Detected\nduring confirmation attempt
note on link
    **Trigger:** confirmBooking() check
    **Condition:** Vehicle became unavailable
    **Action:** Update status = "canceled"
    **Reason:** Another user booked first
end note

active --> canceled : User Abandons\n[voluntary cancellation]
note on link
    **Future Implementation:**
    Explicit cancel endpoint
    for active requests
end note

confirmed --> [*] : Booking Created\n(Archived)
note on link
    Request served its purpose
    Can be deleted or archived
end note

expired --> [*] : Auto-Deleted by TTL
note on link: MongoDB removes expired documents

canceled --> [*] : Archived

note right of active
    **Entry Actions:**
    • Generate unique requestToken
    • Calculate expiresAt = now + 15 min
    • Lock vehicle for user
    • Store priceQuote
    
    **Invariants:**
    • Must have valid user
    • Must have valid vehicle
    • expiresAt > createdAt
    • No overlapping active requests
    
    **Timer:** 15-minute countdown
end note

note right of confirmed
    **Entry Actions:**
    • Mark as confirmed
    • Actual Booking created
    • Lock no longer needed
    
    **Cleanup:**
    • Document can be archived
    • Or deleted (served purpose)
end note

note right of expired
    **Entry Actions:**
    • Release vehicle lock
    • Free for other users
    
    **Auto-Cleanup:**
    • TTL index deletes document
    • No manual cleanup needed
    
    **User Impact:**
    • Must create new request
    • Quote may have changed
end note

note right of canceled
    **Entry Actions:**
    • Release lock immediately
    • Free vehicle for others
    
    **Reasons:**
    • Vehicle became unavailable
    • Conflict detected
    • User voluntary cancel
end note

@enduml
